<p style="font-size:11pt; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:8pt; text-align:justify;">*Figure 1.1: Organizational Structure of Enin Tech Solutions PLC*</p>
<h3 style="color:#27272a; font-family:Arial, sans-serif; font-size:12pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:4pt;">1.6 Company Workflows and Engineering Operations</h3>
<p style="font-size:11pt; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:8pt; text-align:justify;">The engineering departments operate under a hybrid <strong>Agile/Scrum</strong> methodology tailored for fast-paced commercial projects:</p>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**Bi-Weekly Sprints:** Feature requests, client deliverables, and refactoring tasks are scoped into two-week development iterations.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**Daily Stand-Up Sessions:** Engineering teams convene daily for 15 minutes to synchronize on accomplishments, planned tasks, and technical blockers.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**Code Review and Version Control:** All source code is version-controlled via Git. Feature branches undergo mandatory peer review prior to merging into main development streams.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**Continuous Quality Verification:** Dedicated testing gates enforce linting, unit verification, schema integrity checks, and cross-browser responsiveness tests before client deployment.</li>
<hr style="border:0; border-top:1px solid #d4d4d8; margin:14pt 0;" />
<br clear="all" style="page-break-before:always; mso-break-type:section-break" />
<h1 style="color:#e30613; font-family:Arial, sans-serif; font-size:18pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:18pt; margin-bottom:8pt; border-bottom:2px solid #e30613; padding-bottom:4pt;">CHAPTER 2: OVERALL INTERNSHIP EXPERIENCE AND SPECIFIC WORK</h1>
<h3 style="color:#27272a; font-family:Arial, sans-serif; font-size:12pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:4pt;">2.1 Company Selection Rationale</h3>
<p style="font-size:11pt; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:8pt; text-align:justify;">Enin Tech Solutions PLC was deliberately selected by the intern due to its strong market reputation for full-stack JavaScript engineering, production-grade relational database design, and real-world commercial software implementations. The firm provides an ideal environment where academic principles of software engineering can be directly applied to live enterprise projects under close, professional mentorship.</p>
<h3 style="color:#27272a; font-family:Arial, sans-serif; font-size:12pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:4pt;">2.2 Department Placement and Functional Rationale</h3>
<p style="font-size:11pt; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:8pt; text-align:justify;">The author was assigned to the <strong>Web Application Development Team</strong> under the immediate mentorship of <strong>Mr. Andargachew Akalu</strong> (Software Developer). This placement was selected because the author's primary academic specialization and career interest reside in full-stack web engineering, API architecture, and database-driven software solutions.</p>
<h3 style="color:#27272a; font-family:Arial, sans-serif; font-size:12pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:4pt;">2.3 Section Workflow and Agile Team Rituals</h3>
<p style="font-size:11pt; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:8pt; text-align:justify;">Within the Web Application Development Team, daily tasks were orchestrated as follows:</p>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**Sprint Planning & Ticket Breakdown:** Analyzing system requirements received from clients (WOW Burger management) and converting business requirements into technical work tickets.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**Feature Branching in Git:** Creating dedicated feature and bugfix branches (e.g., `feature/order-transactions`, `fix/white-screen-syntax`).</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**Test-Driven Local Verification:** Developing code locally, verifying against MySQL database instances, and running build validation tests.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**Code Audits & Merges:** Submitting pull requests to the immediate supervisor for architectural critique, security vetting, and integration approval.</li>
<h3 style="color:#27272a; font-family:Arial, sans-serif; font-size:12pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:4pt;">2.4 Executed Work Packages and Technical Tasks</h3>
<p style="font-size:11pt; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:8pt; text-align:justify;">During the eight-week internship, the author executed several core work packages for the <strong>WOW Burger</strong> platform:</p>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**Frontend Architecture & Menu Exploration:** Engineered the React component tree for the public portal, including the hero showcase, favorites grid, branch selector, and category navigation tabs.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**Interactive OpenStreetMap Geolocation:** Integrated **Leaflet** and **React-Leaflet** to render physical WOW Burger branches (Bole, Kazanchis, Piassa) with verified coordinates and interactive popups.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**Shopping Cart & Fiscal Calculations:** Developed the global `CartContext` to handle real-time item updates, item removals, slide-out drawer animations, subtotal aggregation, Ethiopian Birr formatting, and statutory 15% VAT calculation.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**Customer Checkout Workflow:** Implemented the client-side checkout form capturing customer credentials, table numbers, and order types (`dine-in` vs. `takeaway`) with strict input validation.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**RESTful API Services:** Programmed modular Express routers and controllers for branches, categories, food products, customer orders, and user accounts.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**Transactional Order Placement Engine:** Implemented atomic database transactions in Node.js/MySQL2 (`beginTransaction`, `commit`, `rollback`) to eliminate orphaned order items and prevent inventory inconsistencies.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**Authentication & Role-Based Access Control:** Configured JWT authentication and Bcrypt password hashing to govern access between Super Administrators and Branch Managers.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**WCAG 2.1 AA Accessibility & Theming:** Integrated dual-theme persistence (light and dark modes) using semantic CSS variables, added keyboard focus traps for modals/drawers, and supplied ARIA accessibility labels across icon buttons and live dynamic regions.</li>
<h3 style="color:#27272a; font-family:Arial, sans-serif; font-size:12pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:4pt;">2.5 Integration of Academic Coursework Knowledge</h3>
<p style="font-size:11pt; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:8pt; text-align:justify;">The assignment provided a direct practical arena to apply theoretical concepts mastered at Haramaya University:</p>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**Object-Oriented & Modular Programming (SEng2011):** Applied in structuring decoupled controllers, service modules, and reusable React UI components.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**Database Systems & Relational Modeling (SEng2032):** Applied in designing third-normal-form (3NF) relational tables, foreign key constraints, composite unique indexing, and ACID transactions in MySQL.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**Web Technologies & Internet Programming (SEng3051):** Applied in crafting responsive HTML5/CSS3 layouts, asynchronous JavaScript promises, DOM manipulation, and REST API design.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**Software Architecture & Design (SEng3081):** Guided the selection of a three-tier decoupled architecture separating presentation, business logic, and data persistence.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**Software Quality Assurance & Testing (SEng4111):** Applied in regression testing, boundary value input validation, API endpoint verification, and headless browser inspection.</li>
<h3 style="color:#27272a; font-family:Arial, sans-serif; font-size:12pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:4pt;">2.6 Programming Languages, Tools, and Methodologies Utilized</h3>
<table border="1" cellpadding="6" cellspacing="0" style="border-collapse:collapse; width:100%; margin-bottom:14pt; border-color:#d4d4d8; font-size:10pt;"><tr style="background:#f4f4f5; font-weight:bold;"><th style="border:1px solid #d4d4d8; padding:6px 10px; text-align:left;">Category</th><th style="border:1px solid #d4d4d8; padding:6px 10px; text-align:left;">Specific Tools / Technologies</th><th style="border:1px solid #d4d4d8; padding:6px 10px; text-align:left;">Application in Internship</th></tr><tr style="background:#ffffff;"><td style="border:1px solid #d4d4d8; padding:6px 10px; text-align:left;">**Languages**</td><td style="border:1px solid #d4d4d8; padding:6px 10px; text-align:left;">JavaScript (ES6+), SQL, HTML5, CSS3</td><td style="border:1px solid #d4d4d8; padding:6px 10px; text-align:left;">Full-stack scripting, schema definitions, and styling</td></tr><tr style="background:#fafafa;"><td style="border:1px solid #d4d4d8; padding:6px 10px; text-align:left;">**Frontend Frameworks**</td><td style="border:1px solid #d4d4d8; padding:6px 10px; text-align:left;">React 18, Vite 5, Tailwind CSS 3</td><td style="border:1px solid #d4d4d8; padding:6px 10px; text-align:left;">SPA UI components, build bundling, and styling tokens</td></tr><tr style="background:#ffffff;"><td style="border:1px solid #d4d4d8; padding:6px 10px; text-align:left;">**Mapping & Icons**</td><td style="border:1px solid #d4d4d8; padding:6px 10px; text-align:left;">Leaflet, React-Leaflet, Lucide-React</td><td style="border:1px solid #d4d4d8; padding:6px 10px; text-align:left;">Geolocation mapping, vector iconography</td></tr><tr style="background:#fafafa;"><td style="border:1px solid #d4d4d8; padding:6px 10px; text-align:left;">**Backend Runtime**</td><td style="border:1px solid #d4d4d8; padding:6px 10px; text-align:left;">Node.js (v24.11.0), Express 5</td><td style="border:1px solid #d4d4d8; padding:6px 10px; text-align:left;">Asynchronous REST server and middleware routing</td></tr><tr style="background:#ffffff;"><td style="border:1px solid #d4d4d8; padding:6px 10px; text-align:left;">**Database**</td><td style="border:1px solid #d4d4d8; padding:6px 10px; text-align:left;">MySQL Server 8.0, `mysql2` Promise Pool</td><td style="border:1px solid #d4d4d8; padding:6px 10px; text-align:left;">Relational storage, indexing, and transactional integrity</td></tr><tr style="background:#fafafa;"><td style="border:1px solid #d4d4d8; padding:6px 10px; text-align:left;">**Security**</td><td style="border:1px solid #d4d4d8; padding:6px 10px; text-align:left;">BcryptJS, JSONWebToken (JWT)</td><td style="border:1px solid #d4d4d8; padding:6px 10px; text-align:left;">Password encryption, token issuance, and verification</td></tr><tr style="background:#ffffff;"><td style="border:1px solid #d4d4d8; padding:6px 10px; text-align:left;">**Dev & Versioning**</td><td style="border:1px solid #d4d4d8; padding:6px 10px; text-align:left;">Git, GitHub, VS Code, PowerShell</td><td style="border:1px solid #d4d4d8; padding:6px 10px; text-align:left;">Version control, branch management, script automation</td></tr><tr style="background:#fafafa;"><td style="border:1px solid #d4d4d8; padding:6px 10px; text-align:left;">**Testing & Inspection**</td><td style="border:1px solid #d4d4d8; padding:6px 10px; text-align:left;">Chrome DevTools Protocol, Headless Chrome</td><td style="border:1px solid #d4d4d8; padding:6px 10px; text-align:left;">DOM mounting verification, console error capturing</td></tr></table>
<h3 style="color:#27272a; font-family:Arial, sans-serif; font-size:12pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:4pt;">2.7 Major Technical Challenges and Bottlenecks Faced</h3>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**Blank White Screen Fatal Render Failure:** The application initially launched on `http://localhost:3000/` with a completely blank white screen. Because the production build passed, static analysis did not immediately reveal the cause.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**Multi-Item Order Integrity Bottleneck:** Early iterations risked partial order writes when network interrupts occurred between inserting the main order record and inserting associated line items.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**Leaflet Bundler Asset Resolution:** In standard Vite bundling, Leaflet's default marker icon images (`marker-icon.png`, `marker-shadow.png`) failed to resolve, resulting in broken image icons on the location map.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**Data Model Role Inconsistencies:** The MySQL database utilized enum values `super_admin` and `manager`, while the existing React frontend authentication guards expected `superadmin` and `admin`.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**Accidental Database Duplications:** Previous manual seed scripts had generated duplicate branch records and product test entries without images.</li>
<h3 style="color:#27272a; font-family:Arial, sans-serif; font-size:12pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:4pt;">2.8 Measures Taken and Implemented Engineering Solutions</h3>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**CDP-Driven Debugging & Syntax Restoration:** Using a headless Chrome inspection script connected via Chrome DevTools Protocol (CDP), the author intercepted an uncaught browser exception:</li>
<p style="font-size:11pt; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:8pt; text-align:justify;">   <code style="background:#f4f4f5; padding:2px 4px; font-family:'Courier New', monospace; font-size:10pt; border-radius:3px;">Uncaught SyntaxError: Unexpected identifier 'cd' at categoryService.js:12</code></p>
<p style="font-size:11pt; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:8pt; text-align:justify;">   A stray <code style="background:#f4f4f5; padding:2px 4px; font-family:'Courier New', monospace; font-size:10pt; border-radius:3px;">cd</code> token had been inadvertently appended to line 12. Removing this token restored the ES module import graph and allowed React to mount successfully.</p>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**ACID Transaction Implementation:** Implemented a transactional block in `orderController.js`:</li>
<p style="font-size:11pt; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:8pt; text-align:justify;">   ```javascript</p>
<p style="font-size:11pt; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:8pt; text-align:justify;">   const connection = await pool.getConnection();</p>
<p style="font-size:11pt; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:8pt; text-align:justify;">   try {</p>
<p style="font-size:11pt; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:8pt; text-align:justify;">     await connection.beginTransaction();</p>
<p style="font-size:11pt; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:8pt; text-align:justify;">     // Insert order record</p>
<p style="font-size:11pt; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:8pt; text-align:justify;">     // Insert all line items in order_items</p>
<p style="font-size:11pt; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:8pt; text-align:justify;">     await connection.commit();</p>
<p style="font-size:11pt; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:8pt; text-align:justify;">   } catch (err) {</p>
<p style="font-size:11pt; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:8pt; text-align:justify;">     await connection.rollback();</p>
<p style="font-size:11pt; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:8pt; text-align:justify;">     throw err;</p>
<p style="font-size:11pt; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:8pt; text-align:justify;">   } finally {</p>
<p style="font-size:11pt; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:8pt; text-align:justify;">     connection.release();</p>
<p style="font-size:11pt; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:8pt; text-align:justify;">   }</p>
<p style="font-size:11pt; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:8pt; text-align:justify;">   ```</p>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**Asset Resolution Fix:** Explicitly imported Leaflet marker assets via bundler imports in `LocationsMap.jsx`, mapping them to `L.Marker.prototype.options.icon` to ensure map pins render properly.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**Middleware Role Normalization:** Added bidirectional role mapping inside `authMiddleware.js` and `userController.js` that dynamically bridges backend database enums with frontend context roles.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**Defensive Schema Auditing & Safe Handling:** Safely audited all database tables using read-only SQL scripts without truncating data, preserving legacy customer records and identifying duplicate records for supervised staging cleanup.</li>
<hr style="border:0; border-top:1px solid #d4d4d8; margin:14pt 0;" />
<br clear="all" style="page-break-before:always; mso-break-type:section-break" />
<h1 style="color:#e30613; font-family:Arial, sans-serif; font-size:18pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:18pt; margin-bottom:8pt; border-bottom:2px solid #e30613; padding-bottom:4pt;">CHAPTER 3: PROJECT SELECTION, PROBLEM IDENTIFICATION, AND IMPLEMENTATION</h1>
<h3 style="color:#27272a; font-family:Arial, sans-serif; font-size:12pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:4pt;">3.1 Project Title and Executive Summary</h3>
<p style="font-size:11pt; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:8pt; text-align:justify;"><strong>Project Title:</strong> *Design and Implementation of WOW Burger Restaurant Management and Digital Ordering Web Application*</p>
<p style="font-size:11pt; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:8pt; text-align:justify;"><strong>Executive Summary:</strong>  </p>
<p style="font-size:11pt; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:8pt; text-align:justify;">The WOW Burger application is a multi-branch web platform tailored for the quick-service restaurant industry in Addis Ababa. The platform automates customer ordering and centralized franchise management. Customers can locate nearby branches (Bole, Kazanchis, Piassa) on an interactive map, browse categorized food and beverage menus with accurate pricing in Ethiopian Birr, customize orders in a digital shopping cart, and submit validated dine-in or takeaway orders. Concurrently, administrative staff utilize an RBAC-protected portal to manage products, categories, branches, user accounts, and track orders through a live, auto-refreshing operational pipeline.</p>
<h3 style="color:#27272a; font-family:Arial, sans-serif; font-size:12pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:4pt;">3.2 Problem Statement and Engineering Justification</h3>
<p style="font-size:11pt; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:8pt; text-align:justify;">Before the implementation of the system, WOW Burger branches relied on traditional manual procedures:</p>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**Physical Menu Constraints:** Printed menus became outdated when seasonal items ran out or market ingredient costs fluctuated.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**Branch Inventory Disconnect:** Customers visiting one branch lacked visibility into menu items exclusive to or unavailable at other branches.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**Order Transcription Errors:** Waitstaff manually recording orders on paper slips caused handwriting misinterpretations, incorrect billing, and incorrect table deliveries.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**Lack of Centralized Metrics:** Franchise owners lacked aggregated visibility into sales volume, order cancellations, and operational speed across locations.</li>
<p style="font-size:11pt; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:8pt; text-align:justify;">Digitizing the restaurant workflow through an accessible, transactional web platform eliminates transcription errors, offers real-time catalog adjustments, enforces exact 15% VAT calculations, and gives management comprehensive operational oversight.</p>
<h3 style="color:#27272a; font-family:Arial, sans-serif; font-size:12pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:4pt;">3.3 Project Objectives</h3>
<h4 style="color:#3f3f46; font-family:Arial, sans-serif; font-size:11pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:10pt; margin-bottom:4pt;">3.3.1 General Objective</h4>
<p style="font-size:11pt; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:8pt; text-align:justify;">To design, implement, test, and deploy a responsive, secure, and accessible digital ordering and restaurant management web application for WOW Burger franchise branches.</p>
<h4 style="color:#3f3f46; font-family:Arial, sans-serif; font-size:11pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:10pt; margin-bottom:4pt;">3.3.2 Specific Objectives</h4>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">To design and implement a responsive customer web portal with dynamic branch menu browsing and search.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">To integrate an interactive OpenStreetMap branch locator utilizing Leaflet.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">To develop an interactive shopping cart drawer that calculates subtotal, 15% Ethiopian VAT, and line-item totals in Ethiopian Birr.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">To build an atomic transactional checkout system for dine-in and takeaway orders.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">To design and normalize a MySQL relational database schema ensuring referential integrity across branches, categories, products, orders, and users.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">To implement a secure Node.js/Express REST API protected with JWT bearer tokens and Bcrypt password hashing.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">To build a role-based administrative dashboard providing operational metrics, catalog management, and a live order queue.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">To ensure universal usability by complying with WCAG 2.1 AA accessibility guidelines and supporting both light and dark visual themes.</li>
<h3 style="color:#27272a; font-family:Arial, sans-serif; font-size:12pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:4pt;">3.4 Development Methodology and Life Cycle Model</h3>
<p style="font-size:11pt; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:8pt; text-align:justify;">The project was executed following the <strong>Agile Iterative Development Model</strong>:</p>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**Requirements Gathering & Analysis:** Collaborated with the supervisor and franchise stakeholders to document functional and non-functional requirements.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**System Architectural Design:** Designed the three-tier architectural layout, REST API route contracts, and third-normal-form (3NF) relational database schemas.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**Iterative Sprint Implementation:**</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">*Sprint 1:* Database initialization, relational schema creation, backend Express setup, and connection pooling.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">*Sprint 2:* Customer-facing frontend views (Home, Menu, Interactive Map, Product Detail Modal).</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">*Sprint 3:* Shopping Cart state management, Birr currency formatting, and checkout form validation.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">*Sprint 4:* Administrative authentication, JWT authorization middleware, and admin dashboard views.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">*Sprint 5:* Transactional order placement, status queue lifecycle, accessibility auditing, and CDP headless browser testing.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**Integration & Verification Testing:** Executed regression testing, API suite validation, and production build bundling.</li>
<h3 style="color:#27272a; font-family:Arial, sans-serif; font-size:12pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:4pt;">3.5 Literature Review and Theoretical Framework</h3>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**Single Page Applications (SPAs):** According to modern web architecture standards (Freeman, 2022), SPAs built with React eliminate redundant full-page browser reloads, loading content dynamically via asynchronous API calls. This drastically reduces server load and delivers a native-app-like user experience.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**RESTful API Principles:** Fielding's (2000) REST architectural style establishes stateless, client-server communication using standard HTTP verbs (`GET`, `POST`, `PUT`, `PATCH`, `DELETE`), enabling clean decoupling between frontend view rendering and backend business logic.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**Relational Integrity and ACID Transactions:** Date (2019) emphasizes that multi-item commercial transactions require Atomicity, Consistency, Isolation, and Durability (ACID). Database transactions ensure that either all components of an order succeed together, or no partial data is written to disk.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG 2.1):** The World Wide Web Consortium (W3C, 2018) guidelines stipulate that web interfaces must be Perceivable, Operable, Understandable, and Robust (POUR). Implementing semantic elements, ARIA labels, and keyboard focus indicators guarantees usability for individuals with visual or motor impairments.</li>
<h3 style="color:#27272a; font-family:Arial, sans-serif; font-size:12pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:4pt;">3.6 Detailed System Architecture and Technical Implementation</h3>
<h4 style="color:#3f3f46; font-family:Arial, sans-serif; font-size:11pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:10pt; margin-bottom:4pt;">3.6.1 Frontend Architecture and Accessible UI Components</h4>
<p style="font-size:11pt; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:8pt; text-align:justify;">The frontend architecture is modularized under <code style="background:#f4f4f5; padding:2px 4px; font-family:'Courier New', monospace; font-size:10pt; border-radius:3px;">frontend/src/</code>:</p>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**Context State Management:** `AuthContext.jsx` manages user authentication tokens, `CartContext.jsx` provides global shopping cart state, and `ThemeContext.jsx` dynamically toggles CSS custom properties for light/dark modes.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**Navigation & Layouts:** `PublicLayout.jsx` wraps customer pages with a skip-to-content accessibility link, sticky header, and footer. `AdminLayout.jsx` provides a responsive sidebar navigation panel.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**Interactive Map:** `LocationsMap.jsx` uses Leaflet to render verified geographic coordinates for Bole (8.99732, 38.78675) and Piassa (9.0317, 38.7533), providing directions via Google Maps links.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**Interactive Cart Drawer:** `CartDrawer.jsx` locks body scrolling, manages keyboard focus trapping, handles quantity updates, and routes the user to checkout.</li>
<pre style="background:#f4f4f5; border:1px solid #e4e4e7; padding:10px; font-family:'Courier New', Courier, monospace; font-size:10pt; line-height:1.2; margin-bottom:12pt; white-space:pre-wrap;">+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                                 App.jsx (Router)                                  |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
       |                                                    |
       v                                                    v
+-------------------------------+                  +-------------------------------+
|         PublicLayout          |                  |     AdminLayout (Protected)   |
+-------------------------------+                  +-------------------------------+
| - HomePage.jsx                |                  | - DashboardPage.jsx           |
| - BranchMenuPage.jsx          |                  | - ProductsPage.jsx            |
| - CheckoutPage.jsx            |                  | - OrdersPage.jsx              |
| - CartDrawer.jsx              |                  | - CategoriesPage.jsx (Super)  |
| - LocationsMap.jsx            |                  | - BranchesPage.jsx (Super)    |
| - Header.jsx & Footer.jsx     |                  | - UsersPage.jsx (Super)       |
+-------------------------------+                  +-------------------------------+</pre>
<p style="font-size:11pt; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:8pt; text-align:justify;">*Figure 3.1: Frontend Application Layout and View Hierarchy*</p>
<h4 style="color:#3f3f46; font-family:Arial, sans-serif; font-size:11pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:10pt; margin-bottom:4pt;">3.6.2 Backend Architecture, Security, and Transactional Processing</h4>
<p style="font-size:11pt; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:8pt; text-align:justify;">Built upon Express 5, the backend modularizes business rules into dedicated controllers:</p>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**`authController.js`:** Handles user login, verifies Bcrypt salted hashes, and issues signed 7-day JWT tokens.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**`orderController.js`:** Coordinates order placement inside atomic MySQL transactions, calculates 15% VAT, and handles status progression (`pending` → `confirmed` → `preparing` → `ready` → `completed` or `cancelled`).</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**`productController.js` & `categoryController.js`:** Deliver branch-filtered catalog querying with automatic fallback to branch 1 if a branch menu is newly initialized.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**`authMiddleware.js`:** Validates Bearer tokens and enforces role-based security boundaries.</li>
<pre style="background:#f4f4f5; border:1px solid #e4e4e7; padding:10px; font-family:'Courier New', Courier, monospace; font-size:10pt; line-height:1.2; margin-bottom:12pt; white-space:pre-wrap;">Customer/Admin Request
         |
         v
+-------------------+      No Token
|   authenticate    |-----------------&gt; [ HTTP 401 Unauthorized ]
|     Token()       |
+-------------------+
         | Valid JWT
         v
+-------------------+      Insufficient
|   requireRole()   |-----------------&gt; [ HTTP 403 Forbidden ]
+-------------------+
         | Authorized
         v
+-------------------+
|  Target Handler   |
|   (Controller)    |
+-------------------+
         |
         v
+-------------------+
|   MySQL2 Pool     |
|   Transaction     |
+-------------------+</pre>
<p style="font-size:11pt; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:8pt; text-align:justify;">*Figure 3.2: Express Security Middleware Pipeline*</p>
<h4 style="color:#3f3f46; font-family:Arial, sans-serif; font-size:11pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:10pt; margin-bottom:4pt;">3.6.3 Database Design, Relational Constraints, and Schema Integrity</h4>
<p style="font-size:11pt; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:8pt; text-align:justify;">The MySQL database <code style="background:#f4f4f5; padding:2px 4px; font-family:'Courier New', monospace; font-size:10pt; border-radius:3px;">wow_burger</code> contains six relational tables:</p>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**`branches`:** `id` (PK), `name`, `address`, `phone`, `is_active`, `created_at`.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**`categories`:** `id` (PK), `branch_id` (FK), `name`, `description`, `created_at`. Enforces `UNIQUE KEY (branch_id, name)`.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**`products`:** `id` (PK), `branch_id` (FK), `category_id` (FK), `name`, `description`, `price`, `image`, `is_available`, `created_at`, `updated_at`.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**`users`:** `id` (PK), `branch_id` (FK), `full_name`, `email` (Unique), `password_hash`, `role` (`super_admin`, `manager`, `staff`), `is_active`, `created_at`.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**`orders`:** `id` (PK), `branch_id` (FK), `customer_name`, `customer_phone`, `order_type` (`dine_in`, `takeaway`, `delivery`), `table_number`, `subtotal`, `vat_amount`, `total`, `status`, `created_at`, `updated_at`.</li>
<li style="margin-left:20pt; margin-bottom:3pt; font-size:11pt;">**`order_items`:** `id` (PK), `order_id` (FK), `product_id` (FK), `quantity`, `unit_price`, `line_total`.</li>
<pre style="background:#f4f4f5; border:1px solid #e4e4e7; padding:10px; font-family:'Courier New', Courier, monospace; font-size:10pt; line-height:1.2; margin-bottom:12pt; white-space:pre-wrap;">+----------------+          +-------------------+          +-----------------+
|    branches    |&lt;----+----|    categories     |&lt;----+----|    products     |
+----------------+     |    +-------------------+     |    +-----------------+
| id (PK)        |     |    | id (PK)           |     |    | id (PK)         |
| name           |     |    | branch_id (FK)    |     |    | branch_id (FK)  |
| address        |     |    | name              |     |    | category_id (FK)|
| phone          |     |    | description       |     |    | name, price     |
| is_active      |     |    +-------------------+     |    | is_available    |
+----------------+     |                              |    +-----------------+
   ^      ^            |                              |             ^
   |      |            +------------------------------+             |
   |      +-------------------------------------------+             |
   |                                                                |
+--+-------------+          +-------------------+                   |
|     orders     |&lt;----+----|    order_items    |-------------------+
+----------------+     |    +-------------------+
| id (PK)        |     |    | id (PK)           |
| branch_id (FK) |     |    | order_id (FK)     |
| customer_name  |     +----| product_id (FK)   |
| total, status  |          | quantity          |
+----------------+          | line_total        |
                            +-------------------+</pre>
<p style="font-size:11pt; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:8pt; text-align:justify;">*Figure 3.3: Relational Database Schema and Foreign Key Associations*</p>
<h4 style="color:#3f3f46; font-family:Arial, sans-serif; font-size:11pt; font-weight:bold; margin-top:10pt; margin-bottom:4pt;">3.6.4 API Module Implementation and Verification</h4>
<p style="font-size:11pt; line-height:1.5; margin-bottom:8pt; text-align:justify;">The REST API was systematically verified using an automated Node.js test harness against the live server:</p>
